O. whereas fisheries are a crucial economic sector for Greenland, providing a livelihood for many; whereas it is essential to ensure sustainable fishing and to safeguard both the marine environment and the future of fisheries, based on the best available scientific advice; whereas it is essential to ensure that negative impacts of trawling on the marine ecosystem are minimised; whereas, according to ICES, the greatest physical disturbance of the seabed and benthic habitats in the Greenland Sea ecoregion is caused by mobile bottom-contacting fishing gear and there is a considerable overlap between the distribution of corals, sponges and sea pens and the areas trawled6 ; whereas according to the ex post and ex ante evaluation study, the management measures applicable to EU vessels operating in Greenland, and the risk levels of EU vessels having negative impacts on ecosystems, mean that bycatch levels and impacts on ecosystems are minimal;

---

6 See the reports ICES reports entitled ‘Greenland Sea Ecosystem Overview’ (2023) and ‘Greenland Sea Ecoregion – Fisheries Overview’ (2024).
